# r1113 P11 regression, boot R1 of world pwgr (plan: feature_writeup/testing/scratch_run_2026-11-13.md section
# "P11 Power Grid regression plan"). Target jar jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-17.jar (sha1
# cbc2ddee37ca4e8f8d844958a9744bc02c148d4a, port phase 10). If a later fix build is named by the orchestrator, use it
# instead and change only the version / count lines of SQ-PWG-P11A.
# Every row block below is copied unchanged from the latest r1113 batch that ran it with fixed probes (source named above
# each block), except: SQ-PWG-68 regex `resistor_value=1(\.00k|000(\.0)?)` and SQ-PWG-06 thyratron heater 6.5 V
# (verdicts/pwg12.md fixes); level-name paths in shell steps rewritten to pwgr. Boot rows -09, -10, -12, -24, -25, -35,
# -36, -45, -46, -47, -55, -62, -67, -72, -76, -84 are superseded by SQ-PWG-P11A (one boot check + the one structure
# placement pass of this world); SQ-PWG-B19N (second nbtall) is dropped: one placement pass per world, B19 is covered
# by SQ-PWG-71.
# Group A superflat, level pwgr, spawn-animals=true (SQ-PWG-61), ground Y -61, blocks at Y -60.
# Areas (no block overlap; all forceloaded by SQ-PWG-P11A):
#   P2 X 990-1060 Z 990-1090 | P3, P4 X 1090-1140 Z 990-1260 | ponder structures X 1290-1970 Z 1290-1320 (removed after)
#   P6 X 1085-1125 Z 1385-1520 | P7 X 1095-1115 Z 1525-1590 | X 1290-1320 Z 1495-1680: -54, -60, -63, -64, -65, -66
#   P9a X 1090-1165 Z 1670-1800 | P9b X 1090-1130 Z 1805-1850 | P9c X 1135-1200 Z 1855-1915 | P9d X 1095-1200 Z 1920-1990
#   P10 X 1095-1135 Z 1995-2085 (rows SQ-PWG-91 to -96 from the runner's P10 gate batch, run after this file)
# Prep (INST = the instance root; all before the boot):
#   COPYDEV=1 PGJAR=$INST/jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-17.jar prep_srv.sh OUT pwgr A spawn-animals=true
#   ls OUT/srv/mods | grep -i -E 'powergrid|cc-tweaked'   (only the -17 jar; cc-tweaked-1.19.2-1.101.4.jar present)
#   for p in pwg_probe pwg_grid_probe pwg_p3_probe pwg_p4_probe pwg_p5_probe pwg_p6_probe pwg_p7_probe pwg_p8_probe pwg_p9a_probe pwg_p9b_probe pwg_p9c_probe pwg_p9d_probe pwg_p10_probe; do
#     cp $INST/tools/scratch_query/$p.js OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_$p.js; done   (thirteen probes, current copies;
#     pwg_p8_probe.js calls BlockState.use directly for the modular display, SQ-PWG-63)
#   ponder datapack from the -17 jar (79 structure files):
#   rm -rf OUT/pwgp; mkdir -p OUT/pwgp OUT/srv/pwgr/datapacks/pwgponder/data/pwgponder/structures \
#     && unzip -o -q OUT/srv/mods/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-17.jar 'assets/powergrid/ponder/*' -d OUT/pwgp \
#     && cp -r OUT/pwgp/assets/powergrid/ponder/. OUT/srv/pwgr/datapacks/pwgponder/data/pwgponder/structures/ \
#     && printf '{"pack":{"pack_format":10,"description":"PWG ponder structures, scratch only"}}' > OUT/srv/pwgr/datapacks/pwgponder/pack.mcmeta
#   mkdir -p OUT/srv/pwgr/computercraft/computer/7 && cp $INST/tools/scratch_query/pwg_p8_cc_startup.lua OUT/srv/pwgr/computercraft/computer/7/startup.lua
#   python3 $INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py toml OUT/srv/config/loadingprotection-common.toml '"Loading Protection Configuration"' protectionDuration 1
#   Default powergrid configs (no edit; R2 and R3 change them).
# Run: qrun.py run OUT tools/scratch_query/batches/r1113pwg/pwgr1.qb perf/runs/r1113/pwgr
#   then the P10 rows on the same server: qrun.py run OUT <runner's P10 gate batch> perf/runs/r1113/pwgr --rows <its
#   setup row>,SQ-PWG-91,SQ-PWG-92,SQ-PWG-93,SQ-PWG-94,SQ-PWG-95,SQ-PWG-96 (not its SQ-PWG-90: P11A did the boot check
#   and the structure pass).
# Then stop the server and continue with pwgr2.qb (same OUT, same world).
# Rows whose last verdict asked for a row-text change not yet in the copied block (judge by the queue text, rerun
# alone if needed): SQ-PWG-49 basin (consumer placed last), SQ-PWG-53 open patch, SQ-PWG-69 (add the 100 ohm load per
# loop), SQ-PWG-70 (overheat cap 185, not 135), SQ-PWG-66 board (build order).
# Probe goggle reads log a RuntimeDistCleaner ERROR (client class): no blanket ERROR reject.
pace 1

## SQ-PWG-P11A | P11 boot check on -17: version, phase 10, registries, 116 recipes, every probe check (P4, P6 to P10), configs, mixins; the world's one structure placement pass
bootexpect Done \(
bootexpect Power grid starting, prepare to be electrocuted \(1\.19\.2 port, phase 10\)
bootexpect Loaded 28 component items
bootreject InvalidInjectionException|InjectionError|Critical injection failure|Mixin apply failed
bootreject ^(?!.*RuntimeDistCleaner).*(/ERROR\]|@Redirect|conflict).*powergrid\.mixins\.json
bootreject Failed to parse component item
> forceload add 990 990 1060 1090
> forceload add 1090 990 1140 1260
> forceload add 1085 1385 1125 1520
> forceload add 1095 1525 1115 1590
> forceload add 1290 1495 1320 1680
> forceload add 1090 1695 1130 1800
> forceload add 1095 1670 1165 1685
> forceload add 1090 1805 1130 1850
> forceload add 1135 1855 1200 1915
> forceload add 1095 1920 1200 1990
> forceload add 1095 1995 1135 2085
> forceload add 1290 1290 1970 1320
sleep 10
> gamerule doMobSpawning false
> gamerule doFireTick false
> weather clear
> zpwg mods powergrid
waitlog \[zpwg\] done 30
> zpwg ns powergrid
waitlog \[zpwg\] ns powergrid total 30
> zpwg3 recipes powergrid
waitlog \[zpwg3\] recipes \d+ 30
> zpwg4 check
waitlog \[zpwg4\] done 30
> zpwg6 check
waitlog \[zpwg6\] done 30
> zpwg7 check
waitlog \[zpwg7\] done 30
> zpwg8 check
waitlog \[zpwg8\] done 30
> zpwg9 check
waitlog \[zpwg9\] done 30
> zpwg9b check
waitlog \[zpwg9b\] done 30
> zpwg9c check
waitlog \[zpwg9c\] done 30
> zpwg9d check
waitlog \[zpwg9d\] done 30
> zpwg10 check
waitlog \[zpwg10\] done 30
> datapack list enabled
> zpwg5 nbtall 1300 -60 1300
waitlog \[zpwg5\] (nbt summary|done) 300
sleep 5
> forceload remove 1290 1290 1970 1320
> powergrid debug problems
shell grep -n -E -A1 'clientMirror|syncWithDoubles|fullStateSynchronizationInterval|solverBackend|splittingsTransformers|overheatedDropChance' config/powergrid-common.toml pwgr/serverconfig/powergrid-server.toml | head -40; grep -c -E 'Mixin apply failed|InvalidInjection' logs/latest.log
expect \[zpwg\] mod powergrid 0\.6\.2-ce-19\.2-17
expect \[zpwg\] ns powergrid block: 78\b
expect \[zpwg\] ns powergrid item: 119\b
expect \[zpwg\] ns powergrid block_entity_type: 60\b
expect \[zpwg\] ns powergrid fluid: 2\b
expect \[zpwg\] ns powergrid menu: 7\b
expect \[zpwg3\] recipes 116$
expect \[zpwg4\] display clutch=true sources on generator_clutch=1$
expect \[zpwg4\] damage spinning_rotor msgId=spinning_rotor bypassArmor=false$
expect \[zpwg6\] fan types .*creativeengineering:dragon_breathing\(500\)
count \[zpwg6\] mixin target \S+ loaded$ == 6
expect \[zpwg9\] tag powergrid:circuit_component missing=\[create:copper_nugget\]
expect file/pwgponder
reject \[zpwg\w*\] (error|config error|\S+ error)
reject InvalidInjectionException|InjectionError|Critical injection failure
reject ^(?!.*RuntimeDistCleaner).*(Exception|/ERROR\]).*(powergrid|patryk)
look every check block matches the pass lines of its gate row apart from counts: zpwg4 = SQ-PWG-35c, zpwg6 = SQ-PWG-46, zpwg7 = SQ-PWG-55, zpwg8 = SQ-PWG-62, zpwg9 = SQ-PWG-67, zpwg9b / 9c / 9d = SQ-PWG-72, -76, -84, zpwg10 = SQ-PWG-90 (B33 tool and loot lines, B34 grid lines); zpwg5 nbt summary files=79 bad=0 error=0 with the three known quirks (device_connector, electromagnet, generator/parallel_windings: SQ-PWG-47's expected list); config grep shows upstream defaults (clientMirror true, overheatedDropChance 0.25, splittingsTransformers present and commented, E4); mixin-failure count 0; `powergrid debug problems` lists none

